WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:04.254
Harriet

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:05.254
Hey Harriet

00:00:05.254 --> 00:00:05.714
Harriet

00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:06.172
Harriet

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:06.923
Oh Harriet

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:07.632
Hey Harriet

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:08.258
Harriet

00:00:08.258 --> 00:00:08.883
Harriet

00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:09.342
Harriet

00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:11.386
Harriet M. Welsch

00:00:11.636 --> 00:00:12.887
I grew up with Harriet.

00:00:12.887 --> 00:00:13.930
I was obsessed with her.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:24.941
I have the great honor of playing Harriet M. Welsch.

00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:28.111
And she’s so unapologetically herself

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:30.947
I’m glad I’m not perfect. I’d be bored to death.

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:33.116
Harriet is kind of all of us in a way.

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:36.077
Like nobody’s perfect; we’re all doing our best;

00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:37.495
I hope people love her for that.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.705
Woo hoo.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:39.164
Huh.

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:41.499
Harriet! Watch where you’re going!

00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:44.044
Ole Golly is Harriet’s nanny.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:46.129
They have a very close relationship.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:48.256
She's very much a mentor.

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:52.343
Remember, life is a struggle and a good spy never quits.

00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:55.805
Ole Golly definitely allows Harriet to be who she is

00:00:55.805 --> 00:00:57.724
and really encourages her and her passion.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.810
Harriet wants to be a writer - more than anything in the world.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:04.147
She doesn’t leave a room without her composition book at her side.

00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:07.484
Ole Golly always told Harriet that in order to be a writer

00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:09.694
you have to know everything.

00:01:09.694 --> 00:01:10.987
And to know everything…

00:01:10.987 --> 00:01:13.448
...you’ve got to see everything.

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:15.366
...and to see everything…

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:18.286
...you’ve got to be a spy.

00:01:18.953 --> 00:01:20.830
Lacey plays Marion Hawthorne

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.291
who is the enemy of Harriet.

00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:25.293
I love getting to play Marion because

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:26.377
she’s really fun to play.

00:01:26.377 --> 00:01:27.378
She’s really funny.

00:01:27.712 --> 00:01:28.755
Need I say more?

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.466
Marion Hawthorne is Harriet’s frenemy,

00:01:31.466 --> 00:01:34.636
the character you really want to not like her,

00:01:35.178 --> 00:01:37.722
but Lacey in this role was

00:01:38.181 --> 00:01:39.057
adorable.

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:41.476
You act like you don’t like me, Harriet,

00:01:41.476 --> 00:01:43.603
but I know your dark little secret:

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.355
You want to be me.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:46.064
Ugh!

00:01:46.314 --> 00:01:48.942
What is great about this series is

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.735
that it is a Valentine to the book.

00:01:50.735 --> 00:01:52.862
It’s as if the characters walked out of the book

00:01:52.862 --> 00:01:54.280
and came onto the screen.

00:01:54.572 --> 00:01:56.574
I read Harriet the Spy as a kid

00:01:56.574 --> 00:02:00.662
and I remember just loving her personality.

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:03.540
There’s no one like you Harriet M. Welsch.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.667
And there probably never will be.

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.168
When I was eight years old reading the book

00:02:07.168 --> 00:02:10.130
for the first time and Harriet was sort of a beacon of hope, 

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.132
of like if she can get through all that,

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.258
I’m going to be ok.

00:02:13.258 --> 00:02:15.802
Between her self esteem, her confidence,

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.929
she was such a role model to me.

00:02:17.929 --> 00:02:20.431
Harriet was the ultimate outsider

00:02:20.431 --> 00:02:23.017
but also who was unafraid to be so.

00:02:23.017 --> 00:02:25.520
And we’re doing it for one thing:

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:26.895
freedom!

00:02:28.356 --> 00:02:30.024
I was so excited when I found out

00:02:30.024 --> 00:02:32.360
that Henson was making Harriet the Spy.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.864
They have a legendary history of bringing complex,

00:02:35.864 --> 00:02:40.201
very beautiful stories for young people specifically to life.

00:02:40.201 --> 00:02:41.995
They’re great storytellers.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:43.288
A lot of the people who work there

00:02:43.288 --> 00:02:45.707
I think are little mini Harriets themselves.

00:02:46.374 --> 00:02:47.834
Whoa!

00:02:49.377 --> 00:02:50.587
[laugh]

00:02:51.045 --> 00:02:53.464
So our Harriet The Spy takes place

00:02:53.464 --> 00:02:55.425
where the original took place which is

00:02:55.425 --> 00:02:57.325
1960s in New York City.

00:02:57.552 --> 00:02:59.721
The show has this retro feel and I think,

00:02:59.721 --> 00:03:00.889
in watching it you’ll feel like

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:02.765
you’ve kind of been transported back there.

00:03:02.765 --> 00:03:06.895
New York City is full of opportunities to learn things.

00:03:06.895 --> 00:03:08.229
It also looks beautiful.

00:03:08.229 --> 00:03:11.441
It’s an animated world that looks amazing.

00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:15.028
It’s so vibrant and the city’s buzzing

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:17.614
and Harriet gets to run around New York -

00:03:17.614 --> 00:03:19.022
it’s almost like her playground.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.784
It’s was a time when kids were allowed

00:03:21.784 --> 00:03:23.620
to have a little bit more free agency.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.247
 We didn’t feel as shy about letting Harriet

00:03:26.247 --> 00:03:27.832
roam the streets of New York City,

00:03:27.832 --> 00:03:31.419
hopping on subways and figuring out her adventures in the city.

00:03:31.419 --> 00:03:31.961
Hey watch where

00:03:31.961 --> 00:03:33.588
you’re going kid!
- Ow!

00:03:33.588 --> 00:03:36.174
I think it’s incredibly important for kids

00:03:36.174 --> 00:03:38.968
to follow Harriet’s lead and be curious about the world.

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:41.429
And I think anyone at any age will enjoy

00:03:41.429 --> 00:03:43.097
going on Harriet’s adventures with her 

00:03:43.097 --> 00:03:45.183
because she’s always looking for the lesson,

00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:46.559
she’s always trying to better herself

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.604
and know everything and you get to know everything

00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:51.356
with her and I think that’s really exciting.

00:03:51.856 --> 00:03:54.943
With the future, there’s so much possibility.

00:03:54.943 --> 00:03:57.237
But if you live in the now

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.656
you can make it something better.

